AI models the pipeline uses
---------------------------

No model weights are included in this repository. model-maker uses the models below; registry/models.toml
lists each one's files, hub revision and licence, and setup.sh downloads them after their licences are
shown. Each object's sidecar says which models made it.

  FLUX.1 [schnell] (Black Forest Labs)          Apache-2.0
    https://huggingface.co/black-forest-labs/FLUX.1-schnell
    Its hub folder holds two text encoders: CLIP ViT-L/14 (OpenAI; MIT) and T5 v1.1 XXL (Google;
    Apache-2.0), shipped there under FLUX.1 [schnell]'s licence.
  BiRefNet                                      MIT (weights and its own model code)
    https://huggingface.co/ZhengPeng7/BiRefNet
    Its backbone is a Swin Transformer, Swin-L (Microsoft; MIT), inside the same weights.
  TripoSG (VAST)                                MIT (the shape model's weights only, at the revision
    https://huggingface.co/VAST-AI/TripoSG       registry/models.toml pins)
    Its image encoder is DINOv2-large (Meta; Apache-2.0), in the same hub folder.
    No code of TripoSG's repository is fetched or run. The weights run with model-maker's own code
    (below), written from diffusers, the TripoSG paper and the weights' tensor names, shapes and
    configuration; its behaviour was confirmed by comparing its outputs with the upstream code's on
    the same inputs, before that code was removed from setup.
  MV-Adapter (SDXL)                             Apache-2.0 (weights and code)
    https://huggingface.co/huanngzh/mv-adapter
    https://github.com/huanngzh/MV-Adapter (its code, checked out at the commit the registry names)
  Stable Diffusion XL base 1.0 (Stability AI)   CreativeML Open RAIL++-M
    https://huggingface.co/stabilityai/stable-diffusion-xl-base-1.0
    The use restrictions of its Attachment A apply to anything made with it. Its hub folder holds two
    text encoders, CLIP ViT-L/14 (OpenAI) and OpenCLIP ViT-bigG/14 (LAION), shipped there under the
    same licence.
  SDXL VAE fp16 fix (madebyollin)               MIT
    https://huggingface.co/madebyollin/sdxl-vae-fp16-fix
  SigLIP 2 So400m (Google)                      Apache-2.0 (the check that a picture shows what was asked for)
    https://huggingface.co/google/siglip2-so400m-patch14-384

Code written after other projects' designs
------------------------------------------

python/model_maker/shape_net.py: the shape model's transformer block and denoiser are our own, written
from diffusers' HunyuanDiT block (Apache-2.0, Copyright The HuggingFace Team; diffusers/models/
transformers/hunyuan_transformer_2d.py) and the TripoSG weights' tensor names and shapes.

python/model_maker/shape_vae.py: the shape model's decoder (latent to field), its attention processor and
its query points' embedding are our own, written from diffusers' AttnProcessor2_0 (Apache-2.0, Copyright
The HuggingFace Team; diffusers/models/attention_processor.py), built on diffusers' Attention,
FeedForward and FP32LayerNorm, and from the TripoSG paper and the weights' tensor names, shapes and
configuration.

Packages the pipeline installs
------------------------------

setup.sh installs the Python packages pinned in python/requirements.lock into this folder's own .venv;
none is shipped in this repository. Some of their wheels bundle shared libraries under other licences
(python/model_maker/check_licences.py lists each one; docs/setup.md, "What the wheels bundle"):

  NVIDIA's CUDA libraries (CUDA runtime, cuBLAS, cuDNN, cuFFT, cuRAND, cuSOLVER, cuSPARSE, cuSPARSELt,
    NVRTC, nvJitLink, NVTX, CUPTI, nvJPEG), in the nvidia-*-cu12 wheels and in torch's and torchvision's:
    NVIDIA's own licences (CUDA, cuDNN, cuSPARSELt). Free to use and to ship with an application; not
    open source.
  libgfortran (numpy, scipy) and libgomp (torch): GPL-3.0-or-later with the GCC Runtime Library
    Exception, which allows shipping them with any program.
  libquadmath (numpy, scipy): LGPL-2.1-or-later. GCC's quad-precision maths, loaded at run time and
    replaceable. It is not part of this repository. It is the one recorded exception to this project's
    no-LGPL rule; see CONTRIBUTING.md, rule 1.

Programs it runs when they are installed
----------------------------------------

  tesseract (Apache-2.0; https://github.com/tesseract-ocr/tesseract), with its English data (Apache-2.0):
    optional. When it is on the PATH, python/model_maker/lettering.py runs it as its own program to read
    each picture try for painted lettering. Neither setup.sh nor this repository installs or ships it;
    a system's package brings it (Debian and Ubuntu: tesseract-ocr), with the Leptonica image library it
    is built on (BSD-2-Clause).
